ignment/claude_audit.md-70----\n--\n/home/ajoe734/code/Lean/audits/oss-alignment/claude_audit.md-104-\naudits/oss-alignment/claude_audit.md-105-**What is only a local contract, not upstream integration:**  \naudits/oss-alignment/claude_audit.md:106:- The contract does not reference any upstream OpenClaw permission API, SDK method, or configuration format.\naudits/oss-alignment/claude_audit.md:107:- `OSS_INTEGRATION_CHECKLIST.md` shows OpenClaw as `not-started`. There is no upstream OpenClaw repo selection, no version pinned, no adapter.\naudits/oss-alignment/claude_audit.md:108:- The local permission model defines *our* policy semantics. It does not demonstrate that we have integrated *upstream OpenClaw's* permission/authorization mechanism.\naudits/oss-alignment/claude_audit.md:109:- If upstream OpenClaw has its own tool-use control system, the local `tool_policy_schema.json` is not yet mapped to it.\n/home/ajoe734/code/Lean/audits/oss-alignment/claude_audit.md-110-\naudits/oss-alignment/claude_audit.md-111-**Missing upstream integration steps:**  \naudits/oss-alignment/claude_audit.md:112:1. Select and pin upstream OpenClaw source.\naudits/oss-alignment/claude_audit.md:113:2. Determine whether upstream OpenClaw has a tool-use permission model or authorization hook.\naudits/oss-alignment/claude_audit.md:114:3. If it does: write an adapter that maps upstream OpenClaw permission semantics → local deny-first model, and document the mapping.\naudits/oss-alignment/claude_audit.md:115:4. If it does not: formally document in `OSS_INTEGRATION_CHECKLIST.md` that OC-001 is a local governance layer *on top of* OpenClaw, not a mapping *from* it.\n/home/ajoe734/code/Lean/audits/oss-alignment/claude_audit.md-116-\n/home/ajoe734/code/Lean/audits/oss-alignment/claude_audit.md-117----\n--\n/home/ajoe734/code/Lean/audits/oss-alignment/claude_audit.md-128-\naudits/oss-alignment/claude_audit.md-129-**What is only a local contract, not upstream mapping:**  \naudits/oss-alignment/claude_audit.md:130:- The schemas are standalone local definitions. They do not reference or derive from any upstream OpenClaw output format.\naudits/oss-alignment/claude_audit.md:131:- `WORK_REBASELINE.md §3` explicitly classifies OC-003 as requiring upstream mapping: \"map upstream OpenClaw outputs into local StrategySpec and workflow handoff objects.\"\naudits/oss-alignment/claude_audit.md:132:- Currently there is no adapter that takes upstream OpenClaw strategy/workflow outputs and converts them to local StrategySpec objects.\naudits/oss-alignment/claude_audit.md:133:- There is no documented field mapping from upstream OpenClaw → `strategy_spec.schema.json`.\n/home/ajoe734/code/Lean/audits/oss-alignment/claude_audit.md-134-\naudits/oss-alignment/claude_audit.md-135-**Missing upstream integration steps:**  \naudits/oss-alignment/claude_audit.md:136:1. Select upstream OpenClaw source (same dependency as OC-001).\naudits/oss-alignment/claude_audit.md:137:2. Inspect upstream OpenClaw's workflow output format (what does it produce after an orchestration run?).\naudits/oss-alignment/claude_audit.md:138:3. Write an adapter: upstream OpenClaw output → local StrategySpec, documenting field-by-field mapping.\n/home/ajoe734/code/Lean/audits/oss-alignment/claude_audit.md-139-4. Document any fields in `strategy_spec.schema.json` that have no upstream equivalent (these are local extensions).\n/home/ajoe734/code/Lean/audits/oss-alignment/claude_audit.md-140-\n--\n/home/ajoe734/code/Lean/audits/oss-alignment/claude_audit.md-149-| 1 | Correct EX-001 status back to `in_progress` / `blocked`; create the missing artifact loader files | Correction | REG-002, FB-003 |\naudits/oss-alignment/claude_audit.md-150-| 2 | P3-001: Define LEAN integration bridge — pin LEAN dependency, fix `_resolve_symbol()` to use real `Symbol.Create()`, write smoke test | Spike / integration task | P3-001 close-out |\naudits/oss-alignment/claude_audit.md:151:| 3 | Select and pin upstream OpenClaw source | Upstrea